WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:02.930
<v Maya>Welcome to part eight, the final part.

2
00:00:02.980 --> 00:00:09.340
<v Maya>We have covered screening, the order of tests, blood pressure, body composition, cardio, strength and endurance.

3
00:00:09.390 --> 00:00:12.160
<v Maya>The last test is test six, flexibility.

4
00:00:12.210 --> 00:00:15.140
<v Maya>Then a full summary, and a twelve question quiz.

5
00:00:15.190 --> 00:00:16.080
<v Dev>Let's go.

6
00:00:16.130 --> 00:00:21.090
<v Maya>There are three categories of flexibility test, just as body composition had three.

7
00:00:21.140 --> 00:00:25.350
<v Maya>Use of a goniometer, visual assessment, and sit and reach tests.

8
00:00:25.400 --> 00:00:27.220
<v Dev>What's a goniometer?

9
00:00:27.270 --> 00:00:30.390
<v Maya>It measures range of motion at the joints, the angle.

10
00:00:30.440 --> 00:00:33.530
<v Maya>It looks like the protractor from a school geometry set.

11
00:00:33.580 --> 00:00:37.230
<v Maya>It has a stationary arm, a moving arm, and a central point.

12
00:00:37.280 --> 00:00:40.300
<v Maya>As the moving arm moves, the angle number changes.

13
00:00:40.350 --> 00:00:43.810
<v Maya>Trainers don't use it, because it needs technical expertise.

14
00:00:43.860 --> 00:00:48.270
<v Maya>Only a physiotherapist or an orthopaedic doctor uses it correctly.

15
00:00:48.320 --> 00:00:54.800
<v Maya>The central point must sit exactly over the joint and the arms along the bones, otherwise the angle is wrong.

16
00:00:54.850 --> 00:00:56.860
<v Dev>So what do trainers do?

17
00:00:56.910 --> 00:00:58.330
<v Maya>Visual assessment.

18
00:00:58.380 --> 00:00:59.590
<v Maya>No device.

19
00:00:59.640 --> 00:01:05.980
<v Maya>Four regions: quadriceps, hamstrings, hip flexors, which are the iliacus and psoas, and the shoulder.

20
00:01:06.030 --> 00:01:08.050
<v Maya>The first three are pass or fail.

21
00:01:08.100 --> 00:01:10.820
<v Maya>The shoulder is graded good, average or poor.

22
00:01:10.870 --> 00:01:12.920
<v Maya>Each side is checked separately.

23
00:01:12.970 --> 00:01:15.540
<v Dev>How is flexibility defined here?

24
00:01:15.590 --> 00:01:19.750
<v Maya>The ability of the muscles to lengthen passively, meaning with outside help.

25
00:01:19.800 --> 00:01:22.960
<v Maya>The trainer is the outside force and assists the client.

26
00:01:23.010 --> 00:01:27.370
<v Maya>If the client still has a huge gap or discomfort despite help, they fail.

27
00:01:27.420 --> 00:01:30.950
<v Maya>And a pass on the right doesn't guarantee a pass on the left.

28
00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:33.000
<v Dev>Is there a common logic?

29
00:01:33.050 --> 00:01:33.890
<v Maya>Yes.

30
00:01:33.940 --> 00:01:38.240
<v Maya>Flexibility is lengthening, so you do the opposite of the muscle's own action.

31
00:01:38.290 --> 00:01:41.380
<v Maya>Quadriceps extend the knee, so you test knee flexion.

32
00:01:41.430 --> 00:01:44.650
<v Maya>Hip flexors flex the hip, so you test hip extension.

33
00:01:44.700 --> 00:01:48.400
<v Maya>Hamstrings are tested with hip flexion with a locked knee.

34
00:01:48.450 --> 00:01:50.170
<v Dev>Quadriceps first.

35
00:01:50.220 --> 00:01:52.680
<v Maya>Client lies prone on the mat, face down.

36
00:01:52.730 --> 00:01:55.100
<v Maya>The trainer helps the heel toward the buttock.

37
00:01:55.150 --> 00:01:57.980
<v Maya>Pass if the heel touches the buttock, each side.

38
00:01:58.030 --> 00:02:00.590
<v Maya>A huge gap despite help is a fail.

39
00:02:00.640 --> 00:02:02.000
<v Dev>Hamstrings?

40
00:02:02.050 --> 00:02:06.380
<v Maya>Client lies supine, one leg at a time, the other leg stays on the floor.

41
00:02:06.430 --> 00:02:10.210
<v Maya>The knee stays locked and the trainer lifts the leg, like a leg raise.

42
00:02:10.260 --> 00:02:14.140
<v Maya>The criterion is above seventy degrees, with ninety being vertical.

43
00:02:14.190 --> 00:02:16.440
<v Maya>Different legs can have different angles.

44
00:02:16.490 --> 00:02:22.740
<v Maya>If one leg reaches eighty and the other stays at sixty despite help, that leg fails and needs stretching.

45
00:02:22.790 --> 00:02:25.410
<v Maya>There is no upper limit, more is simply better.

46
00:02:25.460 --> 00:02:28.680
<v Dev>And I read that the slides say seventy to eighty.

47
00:02:28.730 --> 00:02:29.570
<v Maya>Yes.

48
00:02:29.620 --> 00:02:34.070
<v Maya>The slide says seventy to eighty degrees, the E-book says eighty to eighty five.

49
00:02:34.120 --> 00:02:36.500
<v Maya>The lecture and board say above seventy.

50
00:02:36.550 --> 00:02:38.310
<v Maya>Check your course material.

51
00:02:38.360 --> 00:02:39.800
<v Dev>Hip flexors?

52
00:02:39.850 --> 00:02:43.140
<v Maya>Client lies on a table of decent height, hips at the edge.

53
00:02:43.190 --> 00:02:45.070
<v Maya>One knee is hugged to the chest.

54
00:02:45.120 --> 00:02:47.650
<v Maya>The other leg is suspended over the edge.

55
00:02:47.700 --> 00:02:49.640
<v Maya>The suspended leg is tested.

56
00:02:49.690 --> 00:02:53.300
<v Maya>The pass is when the knee of the hanging leg goes below hip level.

57
00:02:53.350 --> 00:02:56.520
<v Maya>If it stays higher, the hip flexor is stiff or tight.

58
00:02:56.570 --> 00:03:00.890
<v Dev>A student asked, which leg is tested, the hugged or the suspended one.

59
00:03:00.940 --> 00:03:02.620
<v Dev>Why the suspended?

60
00:03:02.670 --> 00:03:06.760
<v Maya>The hugged leg already has the hip flexed, with the hip flexors contracted.

61
00:03:06.810 --> 00:03:13.260
<v Maya>You want to see how much the muscle can lengthen, so you test the suspended leg, which is moving toward hip extension.

62
00:03:13.310 --> 00:03:20.430
<v Maya>The E-book describes a different hip flexor test, lying supine and pulling one knee to the chest, so keep that in mind.

63
00:03:20.480 --> 00:03:21.630
<v Dev>Shoulder?

64
00:03:21.680 --> 00:03:23.120
<v Maya>Standing or sitting.

65
00:03:23.170 --> 00:03:28.570
<v Maya>One hand goes up and behind the head, the other comes from behind and under the opposite shoulder.

66
00:03:28.620 --> 00:03:30.100
<v Maya>Try to touch fingers.

67
00:03:30.150 --> 00:03:32.790
<v Maya>Good, the fingertips touch or hands clasp.

68
00:03:32.840 --> 00:03:34.450
<v Maya>Average, a small gap.

69
00:03:34.500 --> 00:03:36.080
<v Maya>Poor, a large gap.

70
00:03:36.130 --> 00:03:38.660
<v Maya>Check both sides, by switching hands.

71
00:03:38.710 --> 00:03:39.870
<v Maya>Pause and think.

72
00:03:39.920 --> 00:03:44.320
<v Maya>In the hip flexor test, the knee must be above or below the hip for a pass?

73
00:03:44.370 --> 00:03:46.570
<v Dev>Below hip level, or at it.

74
00:03:46.620 --> 00:03:47.200
<v Maya>Yes.

75
00:03:47.250 --> 00:03:52.610
<v Maya>The sit and reach test measures hamstring and lumbar flexibility, the posterior chain.

76
00:03:52.660 --> 00:03:56.450
<v Maya>The client sits and reaches forward, and the farther the reach, the better.

77
00:03:56.500 --> 00:03:57.770
<v Maya>Two methods.

78
00:03:57.820 --> 00:03:59.150
<v Dev>Method one?

79
00:03:59.200 --> 00:04:00.930
<v Maya>The sit and reach box.

80
00:04:00.980 --> 00:04:02.570
<v Maya>A custom made box.

81
00:04:02.620 --> 00:04:05.770
<v Maya>Soles of the feet against the inside wall of the box.

82
00:04:05.820 --> 00:04:06.990
<v Maya>Knees locked.

83
00:04:07.040 --> 00:04:13.010
<v Maya>Bend forward with hands one above the other and push the marker on the top surface as far as possible.

84
00:04:13.060 --> 00:04:17.410
<v Maya>Read the distance in inches on the scale, and look it up for age and gender.

85
00:04:17.460 --> 00:04:19.130
<v Dev>And without a box?

86
00:04:19.180 --> 00:04:21.350
<v Maya>The YMCA sit and reach test.

87
00:04:21.400 --> 00:04:24.070
<v Maya>You need a mat, brown tape and a measuring tape.

88
00:04:24.120 --> 00:04:26.130
<v Maya>The client sits with knees straight.

89
00:04:26.180 --> 00:04:29.280
<v Maya>A brown tape, one foot long, goes heel to heel.

90
00:04:29.330 --> 00:04:36.940
<v Maya>The measuring tape is laid out starting somewhere between the knees, so that the fifteen inch mark lies exactly where it crosses the brown tape.

91
00:04:36.990 --> 00:04:39.740
<v Maya>That fifteen inch point is the zero point.

92
00:04:39.790 --> 00:04:42.770
<v Maya>The client reaches forward, hands one on the other.

93
00:04:42.820 --> 00:04:44.260
<v Dev>Why fifteen?

94
00:04:44.310 --> 00:04:50.200
<v Maya>Everybody should reach at least fifteen inches by default, so the real test is how far beyond fifteen.

95
00:04:50.250 --> 00:04:56.360
<v Maya>And a stiff client who reaches only seven inches still gets a number, because the tape starts between the knees.

96
00:04:56.410 --> 00:05:00.920
<v Maya>With a number, you can set a mid term goal, like reaching the brown tape next time.

97
00:05:00.970 --> 00:05:02.070
<v Dev>Case?

98
00:05:02.120 --> 00:05:05.480
<v Maya>A male, thirty five years, reaches two inches beyond.

99
00:05:05.530 --> 00:05:08.220
<v Maya>Fifteen plus two is seventeen inches.

100
00:05:08.270 --> 00:05:15.960
<v Maya>In the men's twenty six to thirty five column, seventeen falls in the good category, the seventieth and sixtieth percentile pair.

101
00:05:16.010 --> 00:05:17.540
<v Dev>Anything to note?

102
00:05:17.590 --> 00:05:23.650
<v Maya>The E-book adds details, heel spacing, a hold of no more than two seconds, and the best of two trials.

103
00:05:23.700 --> 00:05:25.340
<v Maya>Check your course material.

104
00:05:25.390 --> 00:05:26.290
<v Maya>Recap.

105
00:05:26.340 --> 00:05:32.410
<v Maya>Goniometer for specialists, visual assessment for four regions, sit and reach for the posterior chain.

106
00:05:32.460 --> 00:05:34.320
<v Maya>Let's walk the order once more.

107
00:05:34.370 --> 00:05:37.320
<v Maya>Pre-step: PARQ and informed consent.

108
00:05:37.370 --> 00:05:40.540
<v Maya>One, blood pressure, with the seven step cuff routine.

109
00:05:40.590 --> 00:05:53.600
<v Maya>Two, body composition, eight tests: waist circumference, waist to hip ratio, BMI, skinfold, BIA, Bod Pod, underwater weighing and DEXA, and DEXA is the most recommended.

110
00:05:53.650 --> 00:05:57.250
<v Maya>Three, cardio: Rockport and YMCA step test.

111
00:05:57.300 --> 00:06:00.930
<v Maya>Four, strength: bench press and leg press as relative strength.

112
00:06:00.980 --> 00:06:04.190
<v Maya>Five, endurance: push-up and curl-up, till failure.

113
00:06:04.240 --> 00:06:05.970
<v Maya>Six, flexibility.

114
00:06:06.020 --> 00:06:08.760
<v Dev>And every chart is read the same way.

115
00:06:08.810 --> 00:06:11.290
<v Maya>Yes, by gender, age and the result.

116
00:06:11.340 --> 00:06:14.670
<v Maya>And only a standardised test can be compared to the chart.

117
00:06:14.720 --> 00:06:22.260
<v Maya>The charts come from well accepted research from the United States and other places including parts of Europe, and are accepted globally.

118
00:06:22.310 --> 00:06:23.180
<v Dev>Good.

119
00:06:23.230 --> 00:06:24.760
<v Dev>Let me check a trap.

120
00:06:24.810 --> 00:06:28.190
<v Dev>In the Rockport walk, what's the metronome speed?

121
00:06:28.240 --> 00:06:29.460
<v Maya>There isn't one.

122
00:06:29.510 --> 00:06:33.890
<v Maya>The metronome belongs to the step test, ninety six, and the curl-up, forty.

123
00:06:33.940 --> 00:06:36.290
<v Maya>And no tape is used on the step board.

124
00:06:36.340 --> 00:06:38.740
<v Maya>Tape belongs to the curl-up on the mat.

125
00:06:38.790 --> 00:06:40.990
<v Dev>Five things from this part then?

126
00:06:41.040 --> 00:06:47.070
<v Maya>One, flexibility is the ability to lengthen passively, so the trainer helps and both sides are tested.

127
00:06:47.120 --> 00:06:56.020
<v Maya>Two, quadriceps pass when the heel touches the buttock, hamstrings above seventy degrees, hip flexors with the knee below hip level in the suspended leg.

128
00:06:56.070 --> 00:06:59.970
<v Maya>Three, sit and reach tests hamstring and lumbar flexibility.

129
00:07:00.020 --> 00:07:03.940
<v Maya>Four, the YMCA version sets fifteen inches at the brown tape.

130
00:07:03.990 --> 00:07:07.600
<v Maya>Five, check the rules where sources differ, and use the course version.

131
00:07:07.650 --> 00:07:08.830
<v Maya>Now the quiz.

132
00:07:08.880 --> 00:07:10.230
<v Maya>Twelve questions.

133
00:07:10.280 --> 00:07:13.360
<v Maya>Answer in your head, and we give the answer straight after.

134
00:07:13.410 --> 00:07:14.290
<v Dev>Ready.

135
00:07:14.340 --> 00:07:16.950
<v Dev>Question one, what is a test norm?

136
00:07:17.000 --> 00:07:20.880
<v Maya>A reference sheet that shows where a test score stands for that component.

137
00:07:20.930 --> 00:07:25.430
<v Dev>Question two, what must the PARQ show, and what if there's one yes?

138
00:07:25.480 --> 00:07:26.410
<v Maya>All no.

139
00:07:26.460 --> 00:07:29.920
<v Maya>With a yes, stop, ask, and get a doctor's NOC.

140
00:07:29.970 --> 00:07:33.360
<v Maya>Question three, what's the correct order of the six tests?

141
00:07:33.410 --> 00:07:38.580
<v Dev>Blood pressure, body composition, cardio, strength, endurance, flexibility.

142
00:07:38.630 --> 00:07:45.660
<v Maya>Question four, what is the waist to hip ratio for a waist of thirty six and hips of forty, and is it low risk for a man?

143
00:07:45.710 --> 00:07:52.440
<v Dev>Zero point nine zero, and yes, low risk for a man, because the limit is zero point nine five.

144
00:07:52.490 --> 00:07:58.150
<v Maya>Question five, BMI for sixty three kilograms and one point seven five metres?

145
00:07:58.200 --> 00:08:00.190
<v Dev>Twenty point six, normal.

146
00:08:00.240 --> 00:08:03.010
<v Maya>Question six, why is BMI limited?

147
00:08:03.060 --> 00:08:06.470
<v Dev>It can't tell fat from muscle, and it misses skinny fat.

148
00:08:06.520 --> 00:08:11.850
<v Maya>Question seven, what does BIA rely on, and which is higher in water, muscle or fat?

149
00:08:11.900 --> 00:08:18.320
<v Dev>Water conducts electricity, and muscle is seventy five percent water against ten percent for fat.

150
00:08:18.370 --> 00:08:22.100
<v Maya>Question eight, state the two parts of Archimedes' principle.

151
00:08:22.150 --> 00:08:28.370
<v Dev>Volume underwater equals water displaced, and water displaced equals the buoyant force.

152
00:08:28.420 --> 00:08:32.080
<v Maya>Question nine, the three categories DEXA reports?

153
00:08:32.130 --> 00:08:35.840
<v Dev>Fat free mass, fat mass, bone and mineral mass.

154
00:08:35.890 --> 00:08:42.700
<v Maya>Question ten, the Rockport male case, age fifty, sixty kilograms, fifteen minutes, pulse one hundred and eight?

155
00:08:42.750 --> 00:08:45.920
<v Dev>Forty three point seven eight one, very good.

156
00:08:45.970 --> 00:08:50.590
<v Maya>Question eleven, how is pulse counted in Rockport versus the step test?

157
00:08:50.640 --> 00:08:56.060
<v Dev>Ten seconds times six immediately in Rockport, a full minute after the step test.

158
00:08:56.110 --> 00:09:02.210
<v Maya>Question twelve, which curl-up tape distance for a forty seven year old, and how many beats per repetition?

159
00:09:02.260 --> 00:09:04.540
<v Dev>Eight centimetres, two beats.

160
00:09:04.590 --> 00:09:05.580
<v Maya>That's it.

161
00:09:05.630 --> 00:09:07.860
<v Maya>You've covered the whole of fitness testing.

162
00:09:07.910 --> 00:09:11.030
<v Maya>Standardise, screen, order, and read the chart.

163
00:09:11.080 --> 00:09:13.200
<v Dev>Thanks for listening, everyone.

164
00:09:13.250 --> 00:09:15.170
<v Dev>Good luck with your studies.

165
00:09:15.220 --> 00:09:16.790
<v Maya>Good luck, and keep testing.

